:" ","type":"text"},{"text":"that cell’s value but not yet to the cells below it. A range update applies itself to the","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"O(log ","type":"text"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"n"}],"type":"emphasis"},{"text":") cells that cover the range and leaves it pending there, pushing older pending","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"updates down one level on the way so that updates reach each cell in the order they were made.","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"A query reads without changing the tree, composing the pending updates of the cells it","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"passes through.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"The ","type":"text"},{"isActive":true,"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/RangeTrees\/documentation\/RangeTrees\/MonoidAction"},{"text":" names the monoid and the updates:","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"type":"codeListing","syntax":"swift","code":["enum AddToSum: MonoidAction {","    typealias Values = Sum<Int>","    static var identity: Int { 0 }","    static func compose(_ outer: Int, _ inner: Int) -> Int { outer + inner }","    static func apply(_ update: Int, to sum: Int, count: Int) -> Int { sum + update * count }","}","","var tree = LazySegmentTree<AddToSum>([1, 2, 3, 4, 5])","tree.apply(10, in: 1 ..< 4)","tree.combined(in: 0 ..< 5)   \/\/ 45","tree[2]                      \/\/ 13"]},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"As a collection, a lazy segment tree’s elements are the values, in order, with every update"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"applied."}],"type":"paragraph"}]}],"variants":[{"traits":[{"interfaceLanguage":"swift"}],"paths":["\/documentation\/rangetrees\/lazysegmenttree"]}],"metadata":{"externalID":"s:10RangeTrees15LazySegmentTreeV","remoteSource":{"url":"https:\/\/github.com\/Tyler-Keith-Thompson\/GrafluentCollections\/blob\/main\/Sources\/RangeTrees\/LazySeg